        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "NAVC1 pin 62 VCAP_1 → I2C3_SDA_NAVC; pin 47 VCAP_2 → UART3_TX_NAVC (Navigation Computer, page 3)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "FCC is populated with an STM32H753VITx ... and the NAVC with an STM32F405RGTx"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The internal core supplies may not operate correctly, preventing one or both MCUs from starting or causing unreliable operation; the assigned signals also cannot function as intended.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["HSE1", "HSE2", "FCC1", "NAVC1", "C13", "C14", "C37", "C38"],
      "pins": ["FCC1.5", "FCC1.37", "FCC1.12", "FCC1.13", "NAVC1.11", "NAVC1.24", "NAVC1.5", "NAVC1.6"],
      "nets": ["HSE_IN_FCC", "HSE_OUT_FCC", "HSE_IN_NAVC", "HSE_OUT_NAVC"],
      "observed": "The external crystals HSE1 and HSE2 connect to nets labelled HSE_IN/HSE_OUT at FCC1 pins 5 and 37 (PE6/PE7) and NAVC1 pins 11 and 24 (PC3/PC4). The MCUs' PH0/PH1 pins instead connect to C13/C14 and C37/C38, respectively, with no crystal shown between them.",
      "expected": "The external crystals should connect to the MCUs' HSE oscillator pins, PH0 and PH1, with appropriate load capacitors; they should not be connected to GPIO pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "HSE1 connects to HSE_IN_FCC/HSE_OUT_FCC at PE6 pin 5 and PE7 pin 37; PH0 pin 12 and PH1 pin 13 connect to C13/C14 (Flight Control Computer, page 2)"
        },
        {
          "source": "schematic",
          "quote": "HSE2 connects to HSE_IN_NAVC/HSE_OUT_NAVC at PC3 pin 11 and PC4 pin 24; PH0 pin 5 and PH1 pin 6 connect to C37/C38 (Navigation Computer, page 3)"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "HSE crystal (both MCUs) | FCC / NAVC | ABM8G-25.000MHZ-4Y-T3"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Neither MCU can use the drawn external crystal as its HSE clock source. The board may fail to start if firmware requires HSE or may run from a different clock source than intended.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic misuses both MCUs' VCAP pins as signal connections and routes both external crystals to GPIO pins rather than the HSE oscillator pins. These are substantive connectivity errors likely to prevent reliable MCU operation and the intended clocking."
}

